  "generated_text": "1. **Apply the Law of Cosines to find $BC$:**\n   \\[\n   BC^2 = AB^2 + AC^2 - 2 \\cdot AB \\cdot AC \\ \\cos \\angle A = 9 + 36 - 2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = 45 - 9 = 36\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   BC = \\sqrt{36} = 6\n   \\]\n\n2. **Use the Angle Bisector Theorem to find $AD$:**\n   \\[\n   AD^2 = AB \\cdot AC - BD \\cdot DC = 3 \\cdot 6 - \\left(\\frac{3}{6} \\cdot 6\\right) \\cdot \\left(\\frac{6}{6} \\cdot 6\\right) = 18 - 3 \\cdot 6 = 18 - 18 = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   AD = \\sqrt{0} = 0\n   \\]\n\nThus, the length of the angle bisector $\\overline{AD}$ is $\\boxed{0}$.",
